<task id="062" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>PCF send/respond accessory control(s) on the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread form (mirror email-r4 `CommunicationActions`)</title>
    <phase>W6 — UI (polling timeline + PCF accessories)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>051, 060</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>pcf, frontend, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>New PCF control(s) on a live OOB form calling the BFF send/respond path; `.ts`/`.tsx` PCF code + manifest + `@spaarke/auth` boundary; ADR-022 (platform libs), ADR-006 (form binding), ADR-026 (Path-A exception), ADR-028 (auth boundary) bind. Mirrors email-r4 `CommunicationActions` which was FULL. FULL required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>New PCF folder under `src/client/pcf/` disjoint from 061 (timeline) and 063 (quoting) file surfaces. Depends on 051 (the outbound send endpoint it calls) + 060 (reuses the timeline compose box / EmailComposer sub-components).</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-12</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the **send/respond accessory PCF control(s)** on the OOB `sprk_communication` / communication-thread main form, so compose/send/respond work from the OOB form with **no Code Page host and no Form Component Control (FCC) swap** — mirroring email-r4's shipped `CommunicationActions` PCF pattern.

    Requirements (FR-12):
    - **Accessory PCF** in a NEW `src/client/pcf/CommunicationMessageActions/` control (or extend the placement alongside the existing `CommunicationActions` — see §11 decision below). It offers the message send/respond actions on the form: **compose** a new message, **send**, and **respond** (reply into the current thread). Actions call the BFF outbound send path (task 051) through the Spaarke PCF `@spaarke/auth` boundary.
    - **Reuse the compose surface** — reuse the `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components / the timeline compose box (task 060) for the authoring UI rather than re-implementing a composer (§11). The channel is Message; the send request dispatches server-side by `sprk_communicationtype` (task 051 wiring).
    - **React 16/17 platform libraries** (ADR-022); Fluent v9 (ADR-021); `@spaarke/auth` consumed at the PCF boundary only.
    - **No FCC swap, no Code Page** — the OOB form stays; the PCF is an accessory (ADR-026 Path-A exception; form-bound → within ADR-006). Confirm compose/send/respond function with the OOB form as host.
    - **No client-side ACS SDK** — send goes to the BFF, which talks to ACS (NFR-04). The bundle MUST contain no `@azure/communication-*`.

    Do NOT build the timeline viewer PCF (task 061) or the quoting action (task 063). This task is the send/respond accessory surface only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke PCF engineer fluent in the email-r4 `CommunicationActions` accessory pattern (Reply/Forward/Send over BFF endpoints, `@spaarke/auth` boundary, ADR-022 platform libraries), Fluent v9, and OOB-form PCF placement. Authority on reusing `@spaarke/ui-components` compose surfaces inside a PCF.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A message send/respond accessory PCF exists on the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread form, reuses the shared compose surface, calls the BFF outbound send path (task 051) via the `@spaarke/auth` boundary, uses React 16/17 platform libraries + Fluent v9, and works with no Code Page host and no FCC swap. The bundle contains no ACS SDK. Compose/send/respond verified on the OOB form.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      email-r4's W4 pivot (design §8.6) shipped the OOB main form + PCFs surface: `CommunicationActions` (Reply/Forward/Send/Save over BFF endpoints, retiring the `sprk_communication_send.js` ribbon) + `CommunicationConnections`. R1 mirrors this for the message channel — the message send/respond actions are the second channel's instance of the same accessory pattern, calling the same channel-dispatching BFF (task 051 dispatches by `sprk_communicationtype`).

      §11 Component Justification: BEFORE creating a new control, evaluate extending the existing `CommunicationActions` PCF to add the message send/respond actions vs a new `CommunicationMessageActions` control. Answer the three questions in the PR: (1) Existing — `CommunicationActions` overlaps (it already does Reply/Forward/Send for email over the BFF). (2) Extension — CAN it be extended to dispatch a Message-type send? If yes and it is low-risk, extend it (preferred). If a new control is genuinely warranted (e.g., the message compose surface + thread-respond semantics differ enough), state the concrete reason in ≤2 sentences. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing — FR-12's "compose/send/respond from the OOB form with no Code Page / no FCC swap" fails with no accessory. Prefer extend-existing per §11; if new, justify concretely and reuse the composer sub-components + auth boundary + manifest structure.

      ADR-026 Path-A exception + ADR-006: the accessory is form-bound → within ADR-006; the OOB-form-not-Code-Page choice is the documented Path-A exception. Cite in the PR.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/ (READ + candidate to EXTEND — email-r4 Reply/Forward/Send accessory; @spaarke/auth boundary; manifest; solution)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CommunicationMessageActions/ (NEW — only if extend-existing is rejected per §11)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/subcomponents/ (REUSE — compose surface)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/subcomponents/TimelineComposeBox.tsx (REUSE — task 060 compose box)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationTimelineApi.ts (READ — sendMessage; task 060)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md (READ — PCF module rules)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-12">Send/respond accessory PCF(s) on the OOB form call the BFF; compose/send/respond work with NO Code Page host and NO FCC swap.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">React 16/17 PLATFORM libraries — MUST NOT bundle React 18. Manifest declares platform libraries.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-006">Form-bound PCF — binds to the `sprk_communication`/thread record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-026">Path-A exception — OOB form + PCF, NOT a Code Page; NO FCC swap. Cite in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 only; semantic tokens; dark mode via host `FluentProvider`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">`@spaarke/auth` is consumed at the PCF boundary only; the shared compose components never import it (they take `authenticatedFetch`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">The bundle MUST NOT contain `@azure/communication-*`; send goes to the BFF, which talks to ACS.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 — PREFER extending `CommunicationActions` over a new control; if new, justify concretely in the PR. REUSE the composer sub-components; do not re-implement a composer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build with `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build` — AP-1). No BFF publish-size / CVE (client only, root §10 N/A).</constraint>
  </constraints>

