  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test>From the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread form, composing + sending a new message succeeds via the BFF (mocked/live), with no Code Page host and no FCC swap — no console errors.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Responding (reply into the current thread) from the accessory posts to the BFF and the reply is threaded.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Dark mode: the accessory + compose surface render correctly under the MDA dark theme (Fluent v9 tokens).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>The bundle contains no `@azure/communication-*` (dependency/bundle scan).</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A send/respond accessory PCF is on the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread form; compose/send/respond work with NO Code Page host and NO FCC swap (FR-12).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Actions call the BFF outbound send path (task 051) via the `@spaarke/auth` boundary; the channel is Message (server dispatches by `sprk_communicationtype`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The compose surface reuses `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components / the timeline compose box (grep confirms reuse, not a cloned composer).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Manifest declares React 16/17 platform libraries; React 18 is NOT bundled; the bundle contains no `@azure/communication-*` (ADR-022 / NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` clean; packed + deployed via `pcf-deploy` (or ZIP validated + owner-handoff documented); the §11 extend-vs-new decision is justified in the PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 051 (the outbound send endpoint) + 060 (the compose surface to reuse). Prefer extending the email-r4 `CommunicationActions` PCF (§11) — a second control is only justified if the message respond/compose semantics genuinely diverge; state the reason concretely if so.

    No FCC swap — email-r4's W4 pivot explicitly DROPPED the Form Component Control swap (TASK-INDEX 041 note). Keep the OOB form as host; the PCF is an accessory. Cite the ADR-026 Path-A exception in the PR.
  </notes>

